## 2. Commit Checkpoint Discipline & Sub-Ticket / Phase Traceability (`G3`, `M10`)

### 2.1 When to Commit (`M10` — No Arbitrary WIP Commits)

Agents **never commit arbitrarily mid-phase** ("không thích thì commit, thích thì đặt tên"). A commit is permitted **only** at a verified delivery checkpoint:
1. **Spec Checkpoint**: Right after Gate 1/2/3 approval when `.superpowers/work-items/` is tracked in Git (`docs(<PARENT-TICKET>): record approved spec and plan`).
2. **Sub-Ticket / Phase Checkpoint**: When a **Huly Sub-Ticket** or an approved **Phase (`PHASE-NN`)** has finished implementation, **passed all deterministic CLI verification gates (`PASS`)**, and passed phase review/acceptance (or when the user explicitly requests committing that completed slice).
3. **Stage only task-scoped files**: Always run `git status --short --branch`, stage explicit paths with `git add -- <paths>`, and inspect `git diff --cached` and `git diff --cached --check` before committing. Never run `git add .` or `git commit --no-verify`.

### 2.2 Mandatory Commit Subject Formats (`G3`)

Every commit must follow Conventional Commits and carry explicit **Sub-Ticket** and/or **Accepted Phase (`PHASE-NN`)** traceability:

| Scenario | Mandatory Commit Format | Concrete Example |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Feature has Parent Ticket + Huly Sub-Tickets per Phase/Task** | `<type>(<SUB-TICKET>): <summary> [parent: <PARENT-TICKET>, PHASE-NN]` *(or `Refs: <PARENT-TICKET>, PHASE-NN` in footer)* | `feat({{ticket_prefix}}1201): implement order creation API [parent: {{ticket_prefix}}1200, PHASE-01]` |
| **2. Feature has Parent Ticket + Multi-Phase Breakdown (no separate sub-ticket IDs)** | `<type>(<PARENT-TICKET>): [PHASE-NN] <summary>` | `feat({{ticket_prefix}}1200): [PHASE-02] wire order status SSE stream` |
| **3. Single-Slice Bug Fix / Hotfix with Ticket ID** | `fix(<TICKET>): <root-cause summary>` | `fix({{ticket_prefix}}1245): guard against duplicate idempotency key replay` |
| **4. No Ticket ID (user-supplied requirement)** | `<type>(phase-NN): <summary>` *(only after `PHASE-NN` acceptance)* | `feat(phase-01): implement order creation domain and repository` |
| **5. Breaking Contract Change (`V1`)** | `<type>(<TICKET>)!: <summary>` + `BREAKING CHANGE: <contract impact & D-NN>` | `feat({{ticket_prefix}}1203)!: remove legacy v1 status string [parent: {{ticket_prefix}}1200, PHASE-03]` |

